From 5732005123929ce3b61f58d9c1038e4237b2101e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:57:06 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 call card and settings: media capture state and
 search engine choice for the host

The shell's call card needs to know when a tab uses the camera or the
microphone and to mute them, and its Settings window needs the profile's
default search choices. ABI 1.46 (media_capture, search_engines, bridge
0.48.0) adds both.

Media capture: every registry tab gets a watcher when its services attach.
capturing_video / capturing_audio / capturing_display come from
MediaStreamCaptureIndicator (Chrome's tab recording indicators); camera and
microphone are the page's own report from its media session
(setCameraActive / setMicrophoneActive), with can_toggle_* from the
session's toggle actions. ReArcEngineSetMediaCaptureCallback delivers one
posted event per change, never after tab.closed, and replays non-idle tabs
on registration; ReArcTabGetMediaCapture reads the state.
ReArcTabSetCaptureMuted runs the page's togglecamera / togglemicrophone
handler through content::MediaSession, as Chrome's video-conferencing PiP
buttons do; the engine never disables or stops a track itself.

Search engines: ReArcSearchListEngines returns the engines Chrome's settings
offer as default (TemplateURLService::ShowInDefaultList) with TemplateURLID,
name, keyword, resolved search URL, favicon URL and default / prepopulated /
can-make-default flags; ReArcSearchSetDefaultEngine makes one the
user-selected default. framework.exports and framework.order list the five
new functions. Existing ABI layouts remain unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-06 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
